To launch everything from a clean start

    # 1. Gazebo + robot + controllers (MeArm world, controller_manager, bridges)
    source /opt/ros/lyrical/setup.bash
    source ~/ros2_ws/install/setup.bash
    ros2 launch mearm_description gazebo.launch.py
    
    # 2. In a second terminal — hand tracking + arm control
    source /opt/ros/lyrical/setup.bash
    source ~/ros2_ws/install/setup.bash
    ros2 launch mearm_hand_tracking mearm_hand_tracking.launch.py

  Both are already running right now from this session, so you can just move
  your hand in front of the camera and watch the arm in Gazebo follow it. If
  you ever need to relaunch from scratch, those two commands (in order, giving
  Gazebo a few seconds to come up before the second one) are all you need.

set Hmax,Smax,Vmax all to maximum setting
